Root cause:
The bug was caused by improper memory management in the `mixer_us16x08.c` driver, specifically related to the allocation and deallocation of `usb_mixer_elem_info` objects and associated external objects (`comp_store`, `eq_store`, `meter_store`). The driver did not consistently free allocated memory, leading to memory leaks, and in some cases, it attempted to free memory that had already been freed, resulting in double-free errors. The patch addresses these issues by ensuring that memory is released correctly and only once, and by reorganizing the allocation logic to prevent leaks during error conditions.
